Chapter: LocalNarrowProven

 Third slice of the bounds-prover reach campaign:
 a let-local carries its binding value's
 proven range to a later bounded store. `let n = list-length xs` and
 `let m = n` both keep the 0..2^32-1 range, so storing either into a
 field bounded 0..4294967295 is proven (CDX2053). A local bound to an
 unknown value (a raw parameter) is rejected since CDX2051 became an
 error; that twin lives in errors/narrowing-unproven. This is the
 local-flow the slice-1/2 direct shapes could not reach, since the
 value at the store is a bare name whose binding is one let up.

Section: Definitions

  Meta = record {
   count : Integer between 0 and 4294967295
  }

  measure : List Integer -> Meta
  measure (xs) =
   let n = list-length xs
   in let m = n
   in Meta { count = m }

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
   print-line-uni (integer-to-text ((measure [10, 20, 30]).count))
  end
